  "script": "export const meta = { name: 'finish_review', description: 'Review the retro-futurist landing redesign' };\n\nconst result = await agent(`You are a meticulous UX/frontend reviewer in /home/alex/Projects/ArmchairFuturistLanding. A landing page was redesigned into a \"WORKSTATION '99\" retro-futurist console (late-90s 3D authoring tool): dark CRT hero with Three.js low-poly chrome viewport, terminal boot intro, console chrome frames, IBM Plex Mono labels, chrome-gradient lettering only on dark bars, HP Electric Blue #024ad8 as sole signal color, light HP white-paper body sections.\n\nReview ONLY these files (read them):\n- src/components/sections/HeroSection.tsx\n- src/components/hero/Viewport3D.tsx\n- src/components/hero/TerminalBoot.tsx\n- src/components/hero/sound.ts\n- src/components/ui/console-frame.tsx\n- src/components/sections/KeyStatsSection.tsx\n- src/components/sections/ServicesSection.tsx\n- src/components/sections/CaseStudiesSection.tsx\n- src/components/sections/LaunchTimelineSection.tsx\n- src/components/sections/ConnectSection.tsx\n- src/components/sections/TestimonialsSection.tsx\n- src/lib/section-registry.tsx\n- tailwind.config.ts (the new CRT/theme tokens)\n- src/app/globals.css (the appended WORKSTATION '99 CSS block at file end)\n\nCheck for MATERIAL issues only (not nitpicks):\n1. Accessibility: chrome-text (transparent gradient text) legibility/contrast placement, aria-live usage, button aria-pressed, keyboard paths, reduced-motion handling, focus visibility on dark surfaces.\n2. React/runtime bugs: hooks rules violations, useEffect dependency problems, event listener leaks, Three.js disposal gaps, hydration mismatch risks (matchMedia in effect is OK), incorrect JSX, unused imports that break lint.\n3. Perf: Three.js lifecycle, rAF governance (must pause hidden/offscreen), DPR cap, texture/geometry disposal, marquee patience.\n4. Brief coverage: terminal intro, horizontal scroll gallery, interactive product modules, animated specs, community creations, launch timeline, access CTA, scanlines/pixel/chrome confined tastefully, static fallback on mobile.\n5. Consistency: HP blue stays the only signal color; no neon/cyberpunk drift.\n\nOutput a numbered list of findings, each: [P1 material | P2 polish] file:line — issue — suggested fix. If none in a category, say so. Be terse.`, { model: 'haiku' }).catch(() => null);\n\nreturn result || 'REVIEW_UNAVAILABLE';",
